{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>For I will utterly blot out.</b> First 'blot out' (מחה) in heaven, and afterward 'I will blot out' (אמחה) on earth. And this is what the Rabbis, of blessed memory, said: No nation falls until its patron angel falls first, as is said (Isaiah 34): ״כי רותה בשמים חרבי״ — 'For My sword has drunk its fill in heaven' — ״ואחר כך על אדום תרד״ — 'and afterward it shall come down upon Edom.' <br><b>And in the Midrash:</b> כי מחה — in this world; אמחה — in the World to Come. ״תחת השמים״ — upon them Jeremiah said (Lamentations 3): ״תרדף באף ותשמידם״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:00:28.529304778Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}